lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/IdealSheaf/IrreducibleComponent.lean:14:We define the subscheme structure on an irreducible component of a Noetherian scheme. Typically,
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/IdealSheaf/IrreducibleComponent.lean:16:irreducible component is not already reduced. Instead, we take the closed subscheme defined by
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/IdealSheaf/IrreducibleComponent.lean:17:the kernel of the restriction to the complement of the union of the other irreducible components.
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/IdealSheaf/IrreducibleComponent.lean:18:For example, if `X` is irreducible then this will give back the original scheme `X`.
