lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:10:public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Jacobson.Polynomial
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:14:# Jacobson Rings
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:16:1. Every radical ideal `I` is equal to its Jacobson radical
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:18:3. Every prime ideal `I` is equal to its Jacobson radical
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:19:Any ring satisfying any of these equivalent conditions is said to be Jacobson.
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:20:Some particular examples of Jacobson rings are also proven.
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:21:`isJacobsonRing_quotient` says that the quotient of a Jacobson ring is Jacobson.
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:22:`isJacobsonRing_localization` says the localization of a Jacobson ring
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:23:  to a single element is Jacobson.
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:24:`isJacobsonRing_polynomial_iff_isJacobsonRing` says polynomials over a Jacobson ring
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:25:  form a Jacobson ring.
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:27:Let `R` be a commutative ring. Jacobson rings are defined using the first of the above conditions
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:28:* `IsJacobsonRing R` is the proposition that `R` is a Jacobson ring. It is a class,
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:29:  implemented as the predicate that for any ideal, `I.isRadical` implies `I.jacobson = I`.
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:32:* `isJacobsonRing_iff_prime_eq` is the equivalence between conditions 1 and 3 above.
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:33:* `isJacobsonRing_iff_sInf_maximal` is the equivalence between conditions 1 and 2 above.
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:34:* `isJacobsonRing_of_surjective` says that if `R` is a Jacobson ring and
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:35:  `f : R →+* S` is surjective, then `S` is also a Jacobson ring
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:36:* `MvPolynomial.isJacobsonRing` says that multi-variate polynomials
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:37:  over a Jacobson ring are Jacobson.
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ring.lean:39:Jacobson, Jacobson Ring
