lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ideal.lean:13:# Jacobson radical
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ideal.lean:15:The Jacobson radical of a ring `R` is defined to be the intersection of all maximal ideals of `R`.
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ideal.lean:21:Here we define the Jacobson radical of an ideal `I` in a similar way,
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ideal.lean:28:* `Ideal.jacobson I` is the Jacobson radical, i.e. the infimum of all maximal ideals containing `I`.
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ideal.lean:30:* `Ideal.IsLocal I` is the proposition that the Jacobson radical of `I` is itself a maximal ideal
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ideal.lean:34:* `TwoSidedIdeal.jacobson I` is the Jacobson radical as a two-sided ideal
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ideal.lean:38:* `mem_jacobson_iff` gives a characterization of members of the Jacobson of I
lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Jacobson/Ideal.lean:40:* `Ideal.isLocal_of_isMaximal_radical`: if the radical of I is maximal then so is the Jacobson
